  "app_url": "http://localhost:3000",
  "start_command": "npm --prefix 'output/app' run dev",
  "summary": "Shelf Ledger is a single-user home-library tracker. Users add books (title, author, category), lend them to named borrowers, mark them returned, edit or delete entries, filter to lent-only, and see a summary bar of owned / lent / on-shelf counts. All data persists to localStorage under the key 'shelf-ledger-books' and survives browser refresh. The warm library aesthetic uses cream/parchment backgrounds, burgundy and forest-green accents, and serif headings with a book-spine motif on each card.",
  "implemented_features": [
    "Add a book with title, author, and one of eight categories; the new book appears as available (not lent).",
    "List every owned book in a single card list showing title, author, category, and loan status.",
    "Lend a book by entering a borrower name; status flips to lent and the borrower name is shown.",
    "Return a lent book; it reverts to available and the borrower name is cleared.",
    "Filter toggle between 'All' and 'Lent out' so the user sees only books currently on loan.",
    "Inline edit of title, author, and category on any book; loan status is preserved when unchanged.",
    "Delete a book permanently from the list and persistence.",
    "Summary bar with total owned, currently lent out, and on-shelf counts.",
    "Persistence via localStorage: books, fields, and loan statuses survive a browser refresh.",
    "Invariant enforcement: isLent is true if and only if borrowerName is non-empty on every mutation.",
    "Edge-case handling: empty title/author blocked, empty borrower does not lend, returning non-lent is a no-op, lent-filter empty state, corrupted storage normalized safely."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Single user on a single browser; no authentication or multi-device sync.",
    "localStorage is the persistence layer under key 'shelf-ledger-books', read on startup and written on every mutation.",
    "The predefined category enum is fixed: Novel, Cookbook, Reference, Non-fiction, Biography, Children's, Poetry, Other.",
    "Dates are stored as ISO YYYY-MM-DD using the local date when a book is added.",
    "Book IDs are generated with crypto.randomUUID when available, falling back to a timestamp+random string.",
    "The dev server runs at http://localhost:3000 via 'npm run dev' as configured in vite.config.ts.",
    "Editing a book only touches title/author/category; loan status is intentionally preserved so a user can fix metadata without losing who currently has the book."
  ],
